19. **KNOWN, positive proportion only — Ward–Maestro (2 September 2026), [“Floors for deterministic integer factoring…,” Part 5, Proposition 35.3](https://igent.ai/research/floors-not-bounds/factoring_report_part5_ecm_labels.pdf).** This posted report proves base-2 \(p-1\) success on a positive proportion of pairs with \(x^{1-\varepsilon}<p,q\le x\), at exponents approaching \(1/(4\sqrt e)=0.151632\ldots\). It explicitly distinguishes this from an average bound for an always-completing algorithm.

